Notes:
- The `#[ignore]` suites are the pinned-peer/native-device suites by design; they
  are not counted as passes. T24's added coverage is in `tests/config.rs`,
  `tests/resources.rs` and `tests/cli.rs`.
- `tests/resources.rs::provider_paths_are_confined_to_the_configuration_root`
  covers `../outside.txt`, an absolute path in another temp directory, a legal
  relative path, a legal absolute path inside the root, and an HTTP cache
  `path` escape; `tests/cli.rs::check_rejects_a_provider_path_outside_the_configuration_root`
  proves `--check` exits non-zero for the escape and zero for the legal path.
- `tests/resources.rs::classical_provider_names_unsupported_rule_types_instead_of_dropping_them`
  proves a classical provider with `DSCP` fails with the provider/entry/type,
  and `rule_providers_cover_every_vehicle_and_format` covers
  `PROCESS-NAME-WILDCARD`, `sub.*.middle.example`, IP-CIDR6 and the existing
  vehicles.
- `tests/resources.rs::proxy_provider_override_and_filter_lists_follow_pinned_semantics`
  covers backtick-separated filters, `exclude-type: ss|ssr`, name rewrites,
  `udp`/`skip-cert-verify`/`dialer-proxy` overrides and an unsupported
  `override.tfo` rejection.
- `tests/resources.rs::billow_effective_configuration_registers_cross_task_keys_explicitly`
  and `..._rule_subset_keeps_override_order` replace the earlier hand-written
  "effective config loads" claim.
- `tool/kernel-compat/t24-differential.mjs` keeps the 37-case run; the added
  cases are `src-port-hit`, `ip-cidr6-hit`, `ip-suffix-hit/miss`,
  `ip-cidr-no-resolve-hit` (IP target) and `rule-set-domain-middle-wildcard`.
